PCA:
=>PCA reduces dimensionality while preserving variance
=>Clustering on PCA data is faster
=>Noise is reduced → better cluster separation

Trade-offs of PCA:
=>Reduces dimensions → faster computation
=>Removes noise & redundancy
=>Loss of interpretability
=>Some information loss

Conclusion:
PCA effectively reduced the dataset dimensionality while retaining most of the variance. Clustering performed on PCA-transformed data showed comparable or improved performance based on evaluation metrics. This demonstrates that PCA can enhance clustering efficiency while reducing computational cost, though at the expense of interpretability.